WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.001 line:0%
[ Birds chirping ]

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:05.138 line:0%
-General...thank you
for seeing me.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.172 line:0%
-I figured if there was anyone

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:11.177 line:0%
who could make sense of
this mess, it would be you.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.378 line:0%
-Hello, Neo.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.013
-I know you.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:16.082
-I've tried to keep
my eye on you.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.085
-Oh, beautiful sunset,
beautiful sunset.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.754
-That was the sunset.
-It was worth it.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.623
So, that was a clip
from "Matrix Resurrections."

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:25.825
And I would imagine
one of the things

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.259
with a film like that
is keeping things secret.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:28.561
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.630
-And did you have a lot of
people trying to get it

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.265
out of you or did they respect
that that was something

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.499
they couldn't tell you?

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.235
-Actually, I think everyone
is so terrified --

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.137
or everyone in my vicinity
understands that,

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.807
that nobody
really asked me anything.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.342
Nobody asked me.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.110
Everyone was excited,
but nobody asked me.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.912
I remember,
when I got the script,

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.813
which was the first time
I met Lana Wachowski,

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:49.682
who's, like, a very --

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:53.152
You know, she's a massive
filmmaker and prolific,

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.487
and it was intimidating.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.356
And when she gave me
the script for the first time,

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.658
freshly printed
with my name on it,

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.527
she said,
"Welcome to the Matrix."

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.596
I remember -- I was like --

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.664
And then I took it
and I put it in a vault.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.034
And I swear to God,
I would probably read it

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.437
under covers with,
like, a torch.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.338
"Is anybody watching?"
-That's good.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.106
You took it seriously.
I did.

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:15.875
-You also -- You just shot a
show in London called "Citadel."

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.909
-Yes.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.177
-Tell us a little bit
about that.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:22.148
-Oh, that's really cool.
It's for Amazon Prime Video.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.016
And it's the Russo brothers,

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.753
and it's with Richard Madden,
Stanley Tucci.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.822
It's really cool.
I get to do lots of stunts.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.590
It's a little bit
of a dystopian future.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.525
I'm an international superspy.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.726
-That's perfect.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.695
I want to also ask you,
because, obviously,

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.964
you take care of yourself
and you have a lot of, like --

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:41.534
sort of a self-care regime that
maybe we might not know about,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.203
including something
with beer and eggs.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.305
Tell us what it is
and where you learned it.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.974
-Okay, the Indians would know
about this, by the way.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.675
-Oh, interesting.
-It is, it is.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:52.278
Or at least my mom
claimed that that was true,

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.913
and then I saw her
friends do it, too.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.783
But, apparently, beer and eggs,
which my mom used to do

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.986
when I was growing up,
in her hair,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.754
and she'd leave it as
a conditioner.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.422
And, apparently,
it's really good for you.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.558
It helps with growth,
hair growth.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.393
And it stinks to high heaven,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.460
but when she shampoos it,
it's alright.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.896
-Alright, interesting.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.500
So, do you, like, sort of whip
the egg and then pour a beer in?

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.334
-No, it's not so complicated.
-Okay.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.437
-Just mix it, put the beer in,

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.172
you know,
try to not get it everywhere.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.639
-I feel like you're pranking me,
but I'm gonna do it.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.142
-Google it. I promise you.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.711
-Google it. Alright, sure.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.412
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.014
I know you tried to pick up,
like all of us,

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:31.684
pandemic hobbies,
including painting.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.253
Are you still actively painting

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.920
or have you moved on,
found anything else?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.288
-It lasted two days.

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.891
I painted,
I learned cross-stitch,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:39.992
which was for two days.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.894
I bought a drum set,
'cause I was like,

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:42.895
"I'm gonna do this."

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:43.963
-Oh, no.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.731
-Never sat on it.
-Priyanka, no.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:48.200
-It has my jackets, my clothes.
It looks really great.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.369
So, many, many hobbies --
piano, knitting.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:51.837
I knitted the front half
of a sweater.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.039
-Oh, that's wonderful.
So like a bib. You made a bib?

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.341
-Sort of.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.176
-And it's the size
of my husband's chest,

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:59.445
so it's substantial work,
by the way.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.213
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, of course.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:04.384
-And, so, I didn't really
end up doing very much.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.787
But I wrote a book.
I launched a hair-care line.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.055
-Oh, yeah, Beer and Eggs.
-Yes, Beer and Eggs.

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.858
[ Laughter ]
-I saw that at the store.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.325
I was wondering.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.361
-It's a good name.
-Yeah, it is a really good name.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.628
It was a do-it-yourself kit.

00:03:16.628 --> 00:03:17.864
It was just, like,
some Coors Light

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.098
next to a dozen eggs, yeah.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.033
-There you go. That would sell.
-That would sell.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.135
I mean, that's my favorite --
beer and eggs.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:24.937
-Right?

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.705
I want to ask, as well,

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:30.309
you kind of came up
through the pageant world.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.244
What was your first title
before Miss World?

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:33.546
-Miss India.
-Miss India, okay.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.880
So you're Miss India
and Miss World.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.716
And I'm always fascinated by the
fact that part of it is

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:40.753
asking these giant questions
that would not even be

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:45.992
fair questions to ask, you know,
established adults onstage.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.460
Was that the most terrifying
part of it for you,

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.795
knowing those were coming?

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:53.433
-I think once I stumbled upon
the Miss India pageant --

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.601
Because my mom
thought I was pretty,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.703
and ended up, like a joke,
sending in pictures.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.238
And I actually got a call back.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.807
So I was like, "Oh, this is a
great way of me, like,

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:05.844
skipping my 12th board exams,"
which are, like, serious.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:08.680
So I was like,
"Yeah, let's go for a pageant,"

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.949
never having done it.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.283
Won it. I was 17.

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:12.685
And then I think I just --

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.720
That's when the actress
in me was born.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.189
I just took on the part of,
like, a pageant queen.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:21.994
I used to speak like that.
I was very articulate at 17.

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.329
I had no idea what I was doing,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.864
and it took me
many years, actually,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.833
to sort of shed
the produced image of

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.968
who I thought I needed
to be at that age.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:34.573
And I think, like, women have
these subconscious, like,

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.775
you know, things that are
subliminally put

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:38.510
into their minds,
which is, like,

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.845
this certain way
you have to speak.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:42.415
And pageants kind of do that,
you know, fan that thing.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.250
But it took me many years
to be able to shed that.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.651
But it was very terrifying.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.321
But I'll ask you my question
that I was asked for Miss India.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.988
Let's see what
your answer is, yeah?

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:51.857
-Great.
-Alright.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:54.460
My question was --
This is very "Matrix," actually,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.761
"Blue pill or red pill?"

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:59.265
But "If ignorance is bliss,
then why seek knowledge?"

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.901
-Well, that's a
wonderful question.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.769
[ Laughter ]
-Great way of buying time.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:07.639
-And I don't want you to think
that I am buying time

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:11.043
from this answer,
because I value your time.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:15.214
And I appreciate that this
is a timed answer

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.150
and that, at some point,
a bell will ring

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.220
and I won't have
to get where I was going.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.422
'Cause I can
be bailed out, right, Priyanka?

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:24.823
-No. No, no, no.
-I can't.

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.927
-Millions are watching.
-Great. Add the pressure, guys.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.030
-I would just say to all of you,
on behalf of all of you,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.300
I think that you, too,
have forgotten the question.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.470
And --
-Concentric circles.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.672
And Miss America is Seth Meyers!

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.208
-Oh, my God! Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.978
Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.613
It's always such
a pleasure talking to you.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:50.115
Priyanka Chopra Jonas,
everybody!

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:51.350
"The Matrix Resurrections"

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.285
will be in theaters
and IMAX nationwide

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:54.587
and HBO Max December 22nd.

